      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_a3b84df8bf8879b11ce59acfdb8dfa467e64c00dc5aae8e38cb69c9ddd78a86c",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "For L13, preserving its five listed Noether symmetries yields a parabolic PDE whose scaling coordinate ζ=xe^-2t removes spatial derivatives and leaves Ωtt-Ω=0. Thus the constraint fixes two temporal modes but leaves their amplitudes f1(ζ) and f2(ζ) arbitrary: the coordinate change exposes what the symmetry prescription determines and what it leaves free. As an inference rather than a source statement, this displayed prescription alone supplies no discrete condition on the ζ-dependence. It does not exclude added boundary or global data, nor does it establish a no-go result for other Lagrangians or quantizations. The separate classical transformation z=x²e^{bt} with b=-3 gives z̈=z, explaining why the same reduced time operator appears.",
